WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.202
This tool-selection decision tree is designed for your own project.

00:00:06.202 --> 00:00:09.147
Begin with the question: what capability is missing right now?

00:00:09.147 --> 00:00:14.217
If you need a deterministic calculation or rule, use Python.

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:19.802
If you need internal unstructured knowledge, use retrieval or rag.

00:00:19.802 --> 00:00:25.802
If you need an exact structured fact, use S Q L or an A P I.

00:00:25.802 --> 00:00:30.092
If you need fresh public information, use web search.

00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:37.089
A common bad design is giving the agent three tools called search one, search two, and lookup,

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:41.674
when all three appear to do nearly the same thing.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:45.435
The model then has no clear basis for choosing among them.

00:00:46.209 --> 00:00:50.011
Each tool should represent one distinct capability.

00:00:50.011 --> 00:00:57.701
If two tools overlap heavily, either clarify their descriptions or reconsider whether both are necessary.
